# Wave W17-AC (Route 226): timber post — a timber-works post at the pond’s edge: a weathered post with a stack of sawn log ends laid at its foot, round faces to the road — the design’s DAMBEAVER timber works standing in the prop register (design: the island’s east water works timber at the shore; the works themselves are the water’s, the posts mark where they stand). On east turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s marker posts by the log stack entire: posts mark a road, this one marks a works.
